WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.571 --> 00:00:14.131
and his mom walked up to Aunt Rosa's house.

2
00:00:15.872 --> 00:00:23.374
"I know this isn't ideal," Mom said, "but Aunt Rosa and I have to work Saturday shifts now.

3
00:00:24.034 --> 00:00:26.295
I don't want to leave you home alone."

4
00:00:26.315 --> 00:00:29.576
"But why do I have to stay here with Andre?"

5
00:00:29.956 --> 00:00:30.716
Tim asked.

6
00:00:31.448 --> 00:00:35.531
"He's so much older than me, and we barely even talk when we see each other.

7
00:00:36.312 --> 00:00:37.993
All he does is stay in his room."

8
00:00:38.013 --> 00:00:44.438
"You and your cousin might have more in common than you think," Mom said.

9
00:00:44.458 --> 00:00:47.541
"I doubt it," Tim mumbled.

10
00:00:49.402 --> 00:00:52.364
Inside the house Andre was nowhere to be seen.

11
00:00:53.525 --> 00:00:56.708
Tim plopped down on the sofa and turned on the TV.

12
00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:02.511
"Boring as usual," Tim thought.

13
00:01:02.531 --> 00:01:05.574
"Yo," a voice said suddenly.

14
00:01:05.594 --> 00:01:08.196
"You play the piano, don't you?"

15
00:01:10.138 --> 00:01:10.939
It was Andre.

16
00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:13.762
Tim looked at him, confused.

17
00:01:13.782 --> 00:01:16.404
"Yeah," Tim said.

18
00:01:16.424 --> 00:01:19.988
"Why?" "Follow me."

19
00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:24.252
Andre led Tim toward his room.

20
00:01:27.188 --> 00:01:30.971
Tim realized that he had never seen the inside of Andre's room before.

21
00:01:32.311 --> 00:01:33.452
Several Keep Out!

22
00:01:33.492 --> 00:01:35.734
stickers were crookedly plastered on the door.

23
00:01:39.696 --> 00:01:42.998
to my music studio," Andre said as they entered.

24
00:01:44.799 --> 00:01:45.500
Tim blinked.

25
00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:51.504
It looked like a normal bedroom, not the studios he'd seen in music videos and on TV.

26
00:01:53.804 --> 00:01:59.488
The only musical things he saw were a piano keyboard and a mic connected to Andre's computer via

27
00:01:59.728 --> 00:02:00.729
USB cables.

28
00:02:00.749 --> 00:02:06.312
"It probably doesn't look like much," Andre said, noticing Tim's reaction.

29
00:02:06.332 --> 00:02:11.576
"Many amateur musicians like me set up small home studios.

30
00:02:12.677 --> 00:02:15.839
Recording equipment and software aren't as expensive as most people would think."

31
00:02:15.859 --> 00:02:23.304
"So you record yourself playing the piano and singing on your computer?"

32
00:02:23.748 --> 00:02:24.369
Tim asked.

33
00:02:25.389 --> 00:02:29.192
"Sometimes," Andre said, "but I can do more than that.

34
00:02:30.253 --> 00:02:36.457
With my music program and this keyboard, I can pretty much play any sound I want—real instruments, electronic

35
00:02:36.517 --> 00:02:38.178
sounds, and even dog barks!"

36
00:02:41.641 --> 00:02:42.461
Tim laughed.

37
00:02:45.143 --> 00:02:47.105
"Here, let me show you a song I've been working on."

38
00:02:49.226 --> 00:02:51.608
Andre opened a file on his music program.

39
00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:54.981
"First I came up with this melody.

40
00:02:56.041 --> 00:02:58.822
I played it on the keyboard and chose the sound I wanted to use."

41
00:03:03.024 --> 00:03:05.405
Tim listened to Andre's electronic melody.

42
00:03:06.665 --> 00:03:07.946
"Is that the whole song?"

43
00:03:09.747 --> 00:03:11.968
"No, that's just one track," Andre said.

44
00:03:13.988 --> 00:03:16.630
He pointed to some jagged lines on the computer screen.

45
00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:19.611
"Each instrument I use is on a separate track.

46
00:03:21.191 --> 00:03:24.661
After I made the first track, I added drums and bass."

47
00:03:26.622 --> 00:03:28.623
He played the individual tracks for Tim.

48
00:03:37.087 --> 00:03:39.048
"I can mix the tracks together to make the song."

49
00:03:41.149 --> 00:03:45.552
He pressed Play, and Tim heard all three tracks playing simultaneously.

50
00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:53.722
Tim was surprised by how passionate Andre was about his music.

51
00:03:55.263 --> 00:03:57.544
He'd never seen this side of his cousin before.

52
00:03:58.485 --> 00:03:59.686
"That's so cool!"

53
00:04:00.146 --> 00:04:01.086
he exclaimed.

54
00:04:02.507 --> 00:04:04.969
"Thanks," Andre said with a sigh.

55
00:04:04.989 --> 00:04:08.811
"But I'm not finished yet.

56
00:04:09.471 --> 00:04:11.292
That was just the verse portion of the song.

57
00:04:12.673 --> 00:04:16.836
I can't think of a catchy melody for the chorus—the part that repeats between verses.

58
00:04:18.408 --> 00:04:20.509
That's the part listeners will remember most.

59
00:04:21.450 --> 00:04:22.931
Do you think you can come up with something?"

60
00:04:24.912 --> 00:04:26.913
"Me?" Tim asked nervously.

61
00:04:27.733 --> 00:04:32.616
He'd been playing the piano for seven years, but he'd never composed his own melodies before.

62
00:04:32.636 --> 00:04:36.178
"I guess I can try."

63
00:04:37.399 --> 00:04:41.701
He took a seat at the keyboard and listened to Andre's melody a few more times.

64
00:04:42.381 --> 00:04:45.543
He tried to imagine some possible melodies in his head.

65
00:04:46.544 --> 00:04:50.419
Then he put his fingers on the keys and started to play.

66
00:05:00.127 --> 00:05:01.568
about something like this?"

67
00:05:01.588 --> 00:05:05.431
"Perfect!" Andre looked impressed.

68
00:05:07.293 --> 00:05:11.176
He played the chorus with Tim's melody mixed with the rest of the instruments.

69
00:05:20.864 --> 00:05:26.574
"Now I just need to arrange the parts into an introduction, verses, chorus, and an ending—sort of like

70
00:05:26.594 --> 00:05:27.636
the structure of an essay.

71
00:05:30.461 --> 00:05:31.883
I think I'll start it like this."

72
00:05:53.888 --> 00:05:56.470
"What will you do when you're finished composing the song?"

73
00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:57.530
Tim asked.

74
00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:01.492
"I'm going to rap over it and make a demo song.

75
00:06:02.473 --> 00:06:06.856
Then I'll upload it to the internet and send the link to major record labels.

76
00:06:07.296 --> 00:06:08.536
Maybe they'll give me advice.

77
00:06:09.057 --> 00:06:13.039
Or who knows, if I'm lucky, maybe one of them will offer me a contract."

78
00:06:13.059 --> 00:06:17.522
"You know," Tim said, "I can sing too.

79
00:06:18.382 --> 00:06:21.364
What if you rap the verses and I sing the chorus?"

80
00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:25.102
Andre's face lit up.

81
00:06:25.623 --> 00:06:26.483
"Great idea!

82
00:06:27.705 --> 00:06:29.507
Start writing your own lyrics for the chorus.

83
00:06:30.528 --> 00:06:32.890
I'll finish the song arrangement and write my lyrics too.

84
00:06:33.911 --> 00:06:35.753
Then we can record our vocals."

85
00:06:37.995 --> 00:06:39.657
Tim grabbed a pencil and some paper.

86
00:06:39.677 --> 00:06:45.122
"I guess spending Saturdays with Andre will be pretty fun after all," he thought.
